    "created_at": "2022-06-07T16:52:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-07T16:52:14Z",
    "body": "Right - we map the majority of \"display: -webkit-box\" over to \"display: flex\". There are a few small adjustments:\r\n - min-width/min-height: auto resolves to zero (instead of the auto min-size).\r\n - an auto flex basis resolves to fit-content\r\n - (there are some other things but I think they were for some chrome specific use cases).\r\n\r\nWe also don't use display:flex for -webkit-line-clamp , instead this maps over to block layout (which will be more interoperable for the max-lines property when we can support it). ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
